          "number": 3,
          "letter": "C",
          "english": "The U.S. government's recommended daily allowance (RDA) for the average adult is 50 to 60 grams of protein a day. This may sound like a lot, but Pipitone says: \"We get bits of protein here and there and that really adds up throughout the day.\" Take, for example, breakfast. If you ate two eggs topped with a little bit of cheese and an orange on the side, you already have 22 grams of protein. Each egg gives you 7 grams, the cheese gives you around 6 grams and the orange—about 2 grams. Add a lunch of chicken, rice and broccoli(西兰花), and you are already over the recommended 50 grams. \"You can get enough protein and meet the RDA before you even get to dinner,\" says Pipitone.",
          "chinese": "美国政府为普通成年人的建议每日摄入量（RDA）是每天50至60克蛋白质。这听起来可能很多，但Pipitone说：“我们在一天中的不同时间摄入一点点蛋白质，这些摄入量加起来其实相当可观。”以早餐为例。如果你吃了两个上面放有少量奶酪的鸡蛋，旁边再配一个橙子，那么你已经摄入了22克蛋白质。每个鸡蛋含7克，奶酪含约6克，而橙子含约2克。再加上一份鸡肉、米饭和西兰花的午餐，你摄入的蛋白质就已经超过建议的50克了。Pipitone说：“甚至还没到晚餐时间，你就可以摄入足够的蛋白质并达到RDA的要求。”",
